  "description_short": "Italian dining in George's Botanical Gardens with garden views and classic pasta dishes.",
  "description_long": "Tucked into George's Botanical Gardens on Caledon Street, IL Giardino brings a slice of Italy to the Garden Route. The setting alone—surrounded by greenery and garden pathways—makes this a lovely escape from the everyday. Inside, the atmosphere is relaxed and welcoming, with that easy-going vibe that suits both a casual lunch and a slightly more dressed-up dinner.\n\nThe menu leans into Italian classics: wood-fired pizzas with proper thin bases, hearty pasta dishes, and generous salads. Regulars speak highly of the carbonara and margherita pizza, both done simply and well. Portions are honest, prices are fair, and the service is friendly without fuss. It's the kind of place where you can linger over a glass of wine and enjoy the garden setting.\n\nWhether you're popping in after a stroll through the gardens or looking for a reliable midweek meal in George, IL Giardino offers solid Italian fare in a genuinely pleasant spot. The botanical garden location gives it a peaceful edge that's hard to find elsewhere in town.",
